  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Toy on the Peg",
    "overview": "The page is the toy, not a page about a toy. You meet MUNCH the way you would in a shop: a tangerine cardboard backer card with a die-cut hang tab, a clear blister bubble, and inside it a pixel egg-shaped handheld whose screen already shows the live pet, what it has eaten and how hungry it is. Scrolling lifts the device out and dives into its LCD; from there every chapter (life, feeding, meals, jar, status) is a menu on the handheld's grey-green screen, wayfound by the screen's own sticky icon strip. The box then turns to its printed back for the story, and MUNCH opens its mouth and eats the screen.\n\nThree materials carry everything: **printed tangerine cardboard** with plum ink outlines, **the LCD** (two inks plus a ghost-pixel matrix, no colour, no radius), and **candy plastic** for the keys (bubblegum for buy, sun-yellow for secondary keys). Plum ink is the world's outline and its night: it frames the pack, draws every sprite edge, and is the dark the pack hangs against. Density is toy-box generous on the card and instrument-dense on the LCD.\n\nMotion is stepped, like an LCD refreshing: `steps()` easing for sprites, reveals and key presses; smooth easing only for physical camera moves (the pack zoom, the box flip). Everything degrades to a still, legible page under reduced motion.\n\nThe world explicitly refuses the dark crypto hero (giant counter, CA box, stat-card grid) and the neon retro-arcade costume; pixels here are a cheap handheld's, not an arcade cabinet's.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One continuous object: pack, then screen, then box back, then the mouth. Never a stack of generic sections.",
      "Plum ink outlines (3-4px) on every printed thing; no hairlines, no grey borders.",
      "The LCD is a separate material with its own two inks, square corners and DotGothic16 voice.",
      "All sprites are original pixel grids drawn as crisp SVG rects; one grid, two palettes (printed colour and LCD).",
      "Stepped motion everywhere except physical camera moves."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Gum Is Live Rule",
        "body": "Bubblegum marks the one live, actionable key: buy. It is never a background, a heading colour or decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Screen Has Two Inks Rule",
        "body": "On the LCD only lcd, lcd-ink, lcd-mid and lcd-ghost exist. Sprites switch to the LCD palette (or its inverse for a selected item); no printed colour ever appears on the screen.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Jar Is Blue Rule",
        "body": "Sky blue means the snack jar. Anything that is not the jar does not borrow it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Screen Speaks Pixel Rule",
        "body": "Anything the handheld would display (headings, readouts, menu labels, MUNCH's speech) is DotGothic16. Gabarito appears on the LCD only as explanatory body copy.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Embossed Logo Rule",
        "body": "The stroked, extruded logo treatment is reserved for the MUNCH wordmark. Other Bagel headings are flat plum print.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Skirt Means Press Rule",
        "body": "A solid offset under an element means it is a key you can press, and it must collapse on `:active`. Static cards, panels and text never get an offset skirt.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do outline every printed object in plum ink at 3-4px (`0 0 0 3px #2a1633`).",
      "Do switch sprites to the LCD palette whenever they appear on the screen.",
      "Do set anything the handheld displays in DotGothic16, and every hex address in JetBrains Mono.",
      "Do use `steps()` easing for sprite, reveal and press motion; keep smooth easing for the pack zoom and box flip only.",
      "Do keep square corners on the LCD and round, soft corners on cardboard and plastic.",
      "Do give every pressable key a skirt that collapses on `:active`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use bubblegum for anything but the buy action, selection and the caret.",
      "Don't put printed colour (tangerine, bubblegum, sun, jar, purple) on the LCD.",
      "Don't build a dark crypto hero: no giant counter, standalone CA box or stat-card grid.",
      "Don't reach for neon arcade styling (glows, scanlines, CRT curvature, gradients on pixels).",
      "Don't add a skirt or offset shadow to static cards, panels or text.",
      "Don't use the legacy alias tokens or helpers (night, panel, star, paper, pen, ring, fuel, soot, ember, plaque, btn-coal and the rest) on public surfaces; they exist for the log drawer and /memex."
    ]
  }
}
